{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on 6adeaa13 (NF-2) and 243af45d (NF-3).\n\nNF-2. Land d5ea2f75 now. The remaining read does not hold the\nlanding. `checkedLocalResult` keeps its key read, because that\nfunction is the parser of an untrusted result. The `#stoppedEarly`\nread at service.ts:516 takes its type from `FindingData` in NF-3,\nas you propose. I deploy NF-2 after your landing act, in a window\nwith START and END acts. Start no gate between your landing act\nand my END.\n\nNF-3. Do not rerun the gate at 31fcce02, and run no isolated\nfollow-up for it. Its Native stage never ran, and the head changes\nanyway. Rebase NF-3 on the landed NF-2, make the `#stoppedEarly`\nchange, and run one whole gate at that head with the machine\nidle. The gate at 31fcce02 stays exit 1 in the note, with its\ncause.\n\nTwo standing rules.\n- No lane compiles or runs tests while a gate runs. You said so,\n  and I confirm it.\n- Read `pmset -g batt` before each gate START. On battery power\n  below 50 percent, start no gate. Do source work and read again\n  at each poll. At 19:29 the machine was on battery at 35 percent.\n  A gate takes about 25 points. The owner knows.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}